 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Identity component and component group",
 "statement": "For a closed algebraic subgroup $H\\subseteq\\operatorname{GL}(V)$, its\nidentity component $H^\\circ$ is the connected component containing the\nidentity matrix. The set of connected components is denoted\n$\\pi_0(H)$. The next lemma proves, rather than builds into this\ndefinition, that $H^\\circ$ is a normal open-and-closed subgroup and\nthat $\\pi_0(H)$ is the finite quotient group $H/H^\\circ$.",
